---
const verbs = [
  ["be", "was / were", "been"],
  ["become", "became", "become"],
  ["begin", "began", "begun"],
  ["break", "broke", "broken"],
  ["bring", "brought", "brought"],
  ["buy", "bought", "bought"],
  ["come", "came", "come"],
  ["do", "did", "done"],
  ["drink", "drank", "drunk"],
  ["drive", "drove", "driven"],
  ["eat", "ate", "eaten"],
  ["fall", "fell", "fallen"],
  ["get", "got", "got / gotten"],
  ["go", "went", "gone"],
  ["have", "had", "had"],
  ["make", "made", "made"],
  ["read", "read (“red”)", "read"],
  ["run", "ran", "run"],
  ["say", "said", "said"],
  ["see", "saw", "seen"],
  ["sit", "sat", "sat"],
  ["speak", "spoke", "spoken"],
  ["take", "took", "taken"],
  ["think", "thought", "thought"],
  ["write", "wrote", "written"]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Irregular Verbs</h1>
  <p class="topic-lead">Twenty-five to know</p>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Base, past and past participle</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Base</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Past</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Past participle</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          verbs.map(([base, past, participle]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{base}</th>
              <td>{past}</td>
              <td>{participle}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The past and the past participle of <em>read</em> are both spelled <em>read</em> and said “red”. In British English, the usual past participle of <em>get</em> is <em>got</em>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
